00:20:28.960 --> 00:20:40.440
Lois, what has gotten into you?

00:20:40.440 --> 00:20:44.440
Wait a second, we're not allowed to be up here, Lois.

00:20:44.440 --> 00:20:47.789
Clark?

00:20:47.789 --> 00:20:52.599
Snap out of it.

00:20:52.599 --> 00:20:53.599
You're a hero.

00:20:53.599 --> 00:20:56.599
I'm a regular green arrow.

00:20:56.599 --> 00:20:58.599
Lois, I don't make the news.

00:20:58.599 --> 00:21:00.599
I just report it.

00:21:00.599 --> 00:21:03.599
You are the biggest news there is.

00:21:03.599 --> 00:21:06.599
You're a superhuman being from another planet.

00:21:06.599 --> 00:21:09.599
Okay. Just don't tell human resources, all right?

00:21:09.599 --> 00:21:11.599
Now, I have a deadline to meet.

00:21:11.599 --> 00:21:20.900
Did you just lock us up here?

00:21:20.900 --> 00:21:22.900
Open the door, Clark.

00:21:22.900 --> 00:21:26.279
Lois, it's locked. We need a key.

00:21:26.279 --> 00:21:28.279
Open the damn door, Clark.

00:21:28.279 --> 00:21:29.279
Lois, you...

00:21:29.279 --> 00:21:36.170
Now do you believe me?

00:21:37.170 --> 00:21:40.170
I believe is that this door needs better maintenance.

00:21:40.170 --> 00:21:42.170
Look at the rust in here.

00:21:42.170 --> 00:21:44.170
No wonder I just pull off like that.

00:21:44.170 --> 00:21:45.170
Okay.

00:21:45.170 --> 00:21:46.170
Now we're going to be stuck up here.

00:21:46.170 --> 00:21:47.170
How about this?

00:21:47.170 --> 00:21:53.430
Really listen.

00:21:53.430 --> 00:21:54.430
What are you here?

00:21:54.430 --> 00:22:27.880
That's amazing.

00:22:27.880 --> 00:22:29.880
The acoustics up here are incredible.

00:22:29.880 --> 00:22:32.880
It's like there's some perfect echo point.

00:22:32.880 --> 00:22:33.880
Right here.

00:22:33.880 --> 00:22:35.880
And there's...

00:22:35.880 --> 00:22:36.880
Lois!

00:22:36.880 --> 00:22:46.730
Have you completely lost your mind? That could have really hurt.

00:22:46.730 --> 00:22:48.730
No, it wouldn't, Clark.

00:22:48.730 --> 00:22:49.730
You've got super speed.

00:22:49.730 --> 00:22:52.829
and super strength and super hearing and x-ray vision.

00:22:52.829 --> 00:22:54.029
And I have a deadline, Lois.

00:22:54.029 --> 00:22:56.329
Now, please, if you would excuse me,

00:22:56.329 --> 00:22:59.130
I need to find a way to get off this roof.

00:22:59.130 --> 00:23:43.410
Unless my superpowers include an ability to fly.

00:23:43.410 --> 00:23:44.910
Sorry, guys.

00:23:44.910 --> 00:24:23.339
I'll make sure you get a nice Christmas bonus.

00:24:23.339 --> 00:24:35.990
Thanks, Lex.

00:24:35.990 --> 00:24:37.190
Bravo.

00:24:37.190 --> 00:24:42.150
You found my book and pulled it off in style.

00:24:42.150 --> 00:24:45.400
Looks I could say I've had the pleasure.

00:24:45.400 --> 00:24:47.700
Oh, please, Oliver.

00:24:47.700 --> 00:24:50.079
Ask a billionaire for help and then a vigilante

00:24:50.099 --> 00:25:06.680
deals exactly what I ask for, you need to work on your sleight of hand.

00:25:06.680 --> 00:25:11.680
Now, give me my book, and I'll give you your wish.

00:25:11.680 --> 00:25:13.680
A deal's a deal.

00:25:13.680 --> 00:25:17.680
You know, this isn't just a how-to guide on up in your stage presence.

00:25:17.680 --> 00:25:20.680
There's some really dark stuff in here, Zatana.

00:25:20.680 --> 00:25:22.680
You don't get it.

00:25:22.680 --> 00:25:26.680
The sick irony of my ability is that I can grant so many wishes.

00:25:26.680 --> 00:25:35.029
Everyone's but mine.

00:25:35.029 --> 00:25:36.029
No.

00:25:36.029 --> 00:25:37.029
Please.

00:25:37.029 --> 00:25:40.720
Don't.

00:25:40.720 --> 00:25:49.410
It's the only way I can bring my father back.

00:25:49.410 --> 00:25:50.410
I'm sorry.

00:25:50.410 --> 00:25:57.140
Not good.

00:25:57.140 --> 00:25:59.140
Let I dinyo!

00:25:59.140 --> 00:26:10.319
You don't want to do this.

00:26:10.319 --> 00:26:13.319
You can't just bring someone back and change fate.

00:26:13.319 --> 00:26:15.319
I'm sorry.

00:26:15.319 --> 00:26:17.319
I've waited too long for this.

00:26:17.319 --> 00:26:39.769
I'm coming, Father.

00:26:39.769 --> 00:26:40.769
I'll handle this, Lois.

00:26:40.769 --> 00:26:50.200
Do you speak English?

00:26:50.200 --> 00:26:51.200
Yes.

00:26:51.200 --> 00:26:54.200
You might tell me who you are?

00:26:54.200 --> 00:26:56.200
Lois Lane, Daily Planet.

00:26:56.200 --> 00:26:58.539
I'm sorry. We thought you were.

00:26:58.539 --> 00:27:01.539
We thought you were under some kind of spell?

00:27:01.539 --> 00:27:03.539
Well, she did.

00:27:03.539 --> 00:27:06.170
You know.

00:27:06.170 --> 00:27:11.170
We know Zatanna gave you a wish in exchange for some information on a book.

00:27:11.170 --> 00:27:14.170
I never should have told her how to find that book.

00:27:14.170 --> 00:27:17.170
I'm afraid she's too blinded by her grief to see the danger that she's in.

00:27:17.170 --> 00:27:21.319
Say this woman does no magic.

00:27:21.319 --> 00:27:23.319
What sort of danger are you talking about?

00:27:23.319 --> 00:27:27.319
She must be stopped from using that book to resurrect her father.

00:27:27.319 --> 00:27:29.319
She isn't prepared to make the sacrifice.

00:27:29.319 --> 00:27:31.319
What kind of sacrifice?

00:27:31.319 --> 00:27:37.319
But what I could decipher the incantation to bring a life back required the taking of a life in return.

00:27:37.319 --> 00:27:40.319
So in order to bring her father back, someone else must die.

00:27:40.319 --> 00:27:44.200
A life for a life.

00:27:44.200 --> 00:28:10.720
It is lived from front to back.

00:28:10.720 --> 00:28:13.720
Let death be turned back to front.

00:28:13.720 --> 00:28:16.720
Grant me my wish.

00:28:16.720 --> 00:28:19.720
Resurrect John Zetaire.

00:28:19.720 --> 00:28:23.720
Da' end, Morscha.

00:28:23.720 --> 00:28:32.910
That guy really sounded like you believed in what he was

00:28:32.930 --> 00:28:33.930
saying.

00:28:33.930 --> 00:28:34.930
That's because it was true.

00:28:34.930 --> 00:28:38.930
Now we just need to find Zanada before she tries to give dear old dad one final encore.

00:28:38.930 --> 00:28:41.930
Except you may be too late.

00:28:41.930 --> 00:28:49.920
You're the only person who can get up there and put an end to this right now.

00:28:49.920 --> 00:28:51.920
I know what you're going to say, but...

00:28:51.920 --> 00:28:54.920
No, Clark, there are no butts with you.

00:28:54.920 --> 00:28:56.920
No exception to the room.

00:28:56.920 --> 00:28:59.920
No super leave up there and stop her.

00:28:59.920 --> 00:29:04.680
Look, I don't know.

00:29:04.680 --> 00:29:07.680
Yeah, okay. Okay, Clark, you don't have to know.

00:29:07.680 --> 00:29:09.680
If you won't believe in yourself, then let me believe in you.

00:29:09.680 --> 00:29:10.680
me believe in you.

00:29:10.680 --> 00:29:14.210
I know.

00:29:14.210 --> 00:29:21.210
But deep inside, you don't want to just be a normal guy sitting behind a desk, reporting on disasters.

00:29:21.210 --> 00:29:23.210
Why, you could be out there stopping them.

00:29:23.210 --> 00:29:26.680
Use the power you feel.

00:29:26.680 --> 00:29:32.779
The world needs you.

00:29:32.779 --> 00:29:33.779
You.

00:29:33.779 --> 00:29:47.609
Wait, that's...

00:29:47.609 --> 00:29:48.609
Is it possible?

00:29:48.609 --> 00:29:49.609
Only in your mind.

00:29:49.609 --> 00:29:52.609
Sometimes you just need a little leap of faith.

00:29:52.609 --> 00:29:54.609
Come, Clark.

00:29:54.609 --> 00:29:56.609
You can do this.

00:29:56.609 --> 00:30:00.369
Up, up and away.

00:30:17.500 --> 00:30:20.500
It's Dana. You need to stop this spell.

00:30:20.500 --> 00:30:21.500
Don't move.

00:30:21.500 --> 00:30:23.500
I need to bring my father back.

00:30:23.500 --> 00:30:29.579
At what cost? Are you willing to sacrifice your life for him?

00:30:29.579 --> 00:30:31.579
It's what he did for me.

00:30:31.579 --> 00:30:34.579
He wasn't meant to die.

00:30:34.579 --> 00:30:37.579
I owe him this.

00:30:37.579 --> 00:30:39.579
I know the rules.

00:30:39.579 --> 00:30:45.630
A life for a life. I have to make it right.

00:30:45.630 --> 00:30:49.410
I'm not afraid.

00:30:49.410 --> 00:30:53.410
Do you really think your father would want you to give up the life he gave you to bring him back to you?

00:30:53.410 --> 00:30:54.410
What do you know about?

00:30:54.410 --> 00:30:56.410
Losing the one man who made you who you are.

00:30:56.410 --> 00:31:01.519
The day that I lost my father,

00:31:01.519 --> 00:31:05.930
I thought my world would never be the same.

00:31:05.930 --> 00:31:11.329
It felt like something had been ripped away from me forever.

00:31:11.329 --> 00:31:23.369
Let him go.

00:31:23.369 --> 00:31:25.369
No, it was supposed to be me.

00:31:25.369 --> 00:31:27.369
We don't get to choose.

00:31:27.369 --> 00:31:31.369
But we do get to choose how we live the life that we've been given.

00:31:31.369 --> 00:31:36.039
I'm finally the man that my father wanted me to be.

00:31:36.039 --> 00:32:46.519
Because your father put you to be.

00:32:46.519 --> 00:32:48.519
Peace offering for missing your party.

00:32:48.519 --> 00:32:51.829
Casualties of being a hero.

00:32:51.829 --> 00:32:56.829
Not everyone could have punched through Satana's whammy and saved the day.

00:32:56.829 --> 00:32:58.829
I couldn't have done it without you.

00:32:58.829 --> 00:33:01.829
Thank you for reminding me who I really am.

00:33:01.829 --> 00:33:06.829
Yeah, I guess rebooting your superhero OS rekindled the Chloe fire.

00:33:06.829 --> 00:33:11.829
Looks like a hero support isn't just a day job anymore.

00:33:11.829 --> 00:33:15.829
And for that, we eat bagels.

00:33:15.829 --> 00:33:17.829
Do you remember everything?

00:33:17.829 --> 00:33:20.829
If you're referring to the Just the Fax Man routine,

00:33:20.829 --> 00:33:28.210
it did feel as though a weight had been lifted.

00:33:28.210 --> 00:33:30.210
It must have been hard to harness up again.

00:33:30.210 --> 00:33:33.210
To be honest, the life without responsibility kind of felt empty.

00:33:33.210 --> 00:33:36.210
I mean, this is who I am, Chloe.

00:33:36.210 --> 00:33:38.210
Every morning I wake up with a purpose.

00:33:38.210 --> 00:33:43.210
Yeah, you're not the only one who saw the world through irony-colored glasses.

00:33:43.210 --> 00:33:49.160
Why don't you wait so long to tell me what was going on?

00:33:49.160 --> 00:33:54.569
Space of Clark.

00:33:54.569 --> 00:33:57.569
My life has been a little less than desirable lately.

00:33:57.569 --> 00:34:00.569
I mean, with Jimmy and everything.

00:34:00.569 --> 00:34:01.569
Chloe.

00:34:01.569 --> 00:34:02.569
And I can't understand.

00:34:02.569 --> 00:34:06.569
There's an appeal to the dynamic duo's weekly adventures.

00:34:06.569 --> 00:34:08.570
Well, you haven't missed much.

00:34:08.570 --> 00:34:11.570
Things haven't exactly been smooth between us lately.

00:34:11.570 --> 00:34:15.570
I know you don't want to open a can of kryptonian worms by telling her your secret.

00:34:15.570 --> 00:34:20.570
But whether you like it or not, Lois Lane is a part of your life now.

00:34:20.570 --> 00:34:26.639
Considering the nonstop puppy dog eyes you give her,

00:34:26.639 --> 00:34:32.590
I'm guessing you don't mind much at all.

00:34:32.590 --> 00:34:37.590
Clark, just because you were burned once doesn't mean that you can't give it a second chance.

00:34:37.590 --> 00:34:40.599
Are we still?

00:34:40.599 --> 00:34:41.599
talking about me?

00:34:41.599 --> 00:34:49.460
Are we talking about you and Jimmy?

00:34:49.460 --> 00:34:51.929
Thuchay.

00:34:51.929 --> 00:34:52.929
Okay.

00:34:52.929 --> 00:34:55.929
I'm talking about neither of us living in the past.

00:34:55.929 --> 00:35:01.929
You can never be who you want to be if you're always looking over your shoulder at what could have been.

00:35:01.929 --> 00:35:08.920
Cheers the...

00:35:08.920 --> 00:35:22.010
What is this?

00:35:22.010 --> 00:35:24.010
You dropped by to kick my ass again.

00:35:24.010 --> 00:35:26.010
So much fun for me the first time.

00:35:26.010 --> 00:35:28.010
I came to apologize.

00:35:28.010 --> 00:35:29.010
I just...

00:35:29.010 --> 00:35:30.010
Found by steel.

00:35:30.010 --> 00:35:31.010
Right?

00:35:31.010 --> 00:35:33.010
That's what you said to me backwards, bound by steel?

00:35:33.010 --> 00:35:35.010
I had plenty of time to mull that over when you, uh, you left me.

00:35:35.010 --> 00:35:36.010
You left me.

00:35:36.010 --> 00:35:40.010
there strung up to either die or have my identity revealed.

00:35:40.010 --> 00:35:43.010
I can't ever totally make it up to you or your friends,

00:35:43.010 --> 00:35:47.010
but I would like to try to make sure that something like this doesn't happen again.

00:35:47.010 --> 00:35:51.710
Here's a thought. Don't do it again.

00:35:51.710 --> 00:35:52.710
Hold on.

00:35:52.710 --> 00:35:53.710
Just a second.

00:35:53.710 --> 00:36:06.760
I know how difficult the sacrifices you made must have been,

00:36:06.760 --> 00:36:09.760
especially considering how hell bent you were on getting what you wanted.

00:36:09.760 --> 00:36:16.139
Anyway, in the end, you made the tough choice, and, um, I can respect that.

00:36:16.139 --> 00:36:20.849
Just no.

00:36:20.849 --> 00:36:21.849
No.

00:36:21.849 --> 00:36:24.849
Well, there are far more dangerous people out there in the world than me.

00:36:24.849 --> 00:36:28.849
People with much greater control of the genuinely nasty magics than I do.

00:36:28.849 --> 00:36:35.360
So, if you ever run into my kind of mischief again,

00:36:35.360 --> 00:36:38.360
call me.

00:36:38.360 --> 00:36:42.360
And wherever I am, this time I'm on your side.

00:36:42.360 --> 00:36:46.360
So I guess this means you're taking your show on the road.

00:36:46.360 --> 00:36:50.360
Thinking about taking a little bit of time off to do some late reading.

00:36:50.360 --> 00:36:53.360
If I'm ever going to do my father part,

00:36:53.360 --> 00:36:56.360
I've got a lot of catching up to do.

00:36:56.360 --> 00:37:09.780
So, what, what is this exactly, some kind of magic spell to summon you?

00:37:09.780 --> 00:37:13.780
I just hold it up, say your name a couple times, and poof you appear?

00:37:13.780 --> 00:37:15.780
It's my phone number.

00:37:15.780 --> 00:37:53.329
Is there something on your mind, Lois?

00:37:53.329 --> 00:38:00.349
So how long did it take for you to realize that I wasn't my usual charming self?

00:38:00.349 --> 00:38:03.349
Well, I have to admit, I should have picked up on it sooner.

00:38:03.349 --> 00:38:06.349
You weren't as bossy as usual.

00:38:06.349 --> 00:38:09.349
And Chloe let me drive.

00:38:09.349 --> 00:38:16.659
Well, little blonde sources tell me that you don't mind my assertive flair.

00:38:16.659 --> 00:38:22.909
Let me see it.

00:38:22.909 --> 00:38:26.639
Lois, I don't know what you're talking about.

00:38:26.639 --> 00:38:32.320
You have a terrible poker face model.

00:38:32.320 --> 00:38:53.969
Give me, give me.

00:38:53.969 --> 00:38:58.789
Who would have known you were this sentimental?

00:38:58.789 --> 00:39:02.789
We should hang it up so that everyone can see it.

00:39:02.789 --> 00:39:05.789
This is a momento from my first day on the job.

00:39:05.789 --> 00:39:14.739
In a constant reminder, there's only one low slain.

00:39:14.739 --> 00:39:15.739
You better believe it.

00:39:15.739 --> 00:39:22.670
A big night?

00:39:22.670 --> 00:39:24.670
Hmm. Yeah, this guy in first class asked me out,

00:39:24.670 --> 00:39:26.670
and I figured why the hell not, right?

00:39:26.670 --> 00:39:33.920
What about you? Big plans?

00:39:33.920 --> 00:39:37.920
I'm just gonna hang around here, you know, follow up in a few things.

00:39:37.920 --> 00:39:39.920
Do you want me to call you if anything comes through the wire?

00:39:39.920 --> 00:39:40.920
See if you're available?

00:39:40.920 --> 00:39:44.199
You mean if you want to stand me up again?

00:39:44.199 --> 00:39:45.199
Lois, that was...

00:39:45.199 --> 00:39:47.199
A mistake. Agreed.

00:39:47.199 --> 00:39:51.199
Why don't we just table this whole office thrown together in the trenches, sparks thing?

00:39:51.199 --> 00:39:54.199
Okay? Back to basics. Keep the game on the field.

00:39:54.199 --> 00:39:57.760
Yeah, it's a good rule.

00:39:57.760 --> 00:40:02.380
You should.

00:40:02.380 --> 00:40:03.380
I should add that to the list.

00:40:03.380 --> 00:40:21.630
Ready?

00:40:21.630 --> 00:40:23.630
Ready as you are.

00:40:23.630 --> 00:40:24.630
Chloe.

00:40:24.630 --> 00:40:27.630
This will mean leaving your old life as a reporter behind.

00:40:27.630 --> 00:40:31.630
You sure you want to say goodbye to that forever?

00:40:31.630 --> 00:40:36.630
You know, yesterday I wouldn't have been able to answer that question.

00:40:36.630 --> 00:40:39.630
But after spending the day at the Daily Planet, I realized...

00:40:39.630 --> 00:40:50.289
That's interesting, everyone seems to have so much clarity after a dose of the Zatana dust.

00:40:50.289 --> 00:40:56.179
It almost makes me wish I had my turn at the magic lamp, too.

00:40:56.179 --> 00:40:57.179
I'll save you the human.

00:40:57.179 --> 00:40:59.179
No blisters.

00:40:59.179 --> 00:41:01.179
You already know what you really want.

00:41:01.179 --> 00:41:02.179
We all do.

00:41:02.179 --> 00:41:04.179
We just don't listen.

00:41:04.179 --> 00:41:08.449
And you're sure this is it.

00:41:08.449 --> 00:41:11.949
This is where I belong.

00:41:11.949 --> 00:41:24.219
Canary, online.

00:41:24.219 --> 00:41:26.219
Cyborg, online.

00:41:26.219 --> 00:41:29.219
Impulse, online.

00:41:29.219 --> 00:41:30.219
Arrow, online.

00:41:30.219 --> 00:41:39.739
It was officially online.

